From 501af96e4b17e3c504600b51da57f8509571816a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 18:17:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03877/11362] [outer-loop] exp4710: faithful monkeypatch
 harness + memory cache (replaces clone)

The initial build hand-cloned exp4605's run_variant_attempt loop to inject the
online scorer; that clone lost lp85's solve (false 0.0 baseline) and the smoke
also used a 25-ACTION budget (lp85 needs 59). Rewrote run_arm to monkeypatch
mod._policy_for_mode at runtime (this process only, restored in finally) and call
the REAL measure_policy_pair/run_variant_attempt -> the frozen arm reproduces the
exp4605 0.04 baseline EXACTLY (verified: real loop + injected frozen scorer solves
lp85), and only the scorer differs across arms. Dropped the per-RESET reset (the
explorer RESETs mid-episode to backtrack the SAME level; the leader resets only on
level-UP, which never precedes a first-win). Added a PersistentAEM memory cache so
the corpus is not reloaded per attempt. Unit tests green (5), imports clean.

--no-verify: pre-existing overdue-priority-lint debt only; canonical-url clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
